</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Drobny</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Freissmuth</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cholera toxin induces cyclic AMP-independent down-regulation of Gs alpha and sensitization of alpha 2-autoreceptors in chick sympathetic neurons</article-title><source>J Neurochem</source><year>1996</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>1019</fpage><lpage>1026</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8769862</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shen</surname><given-names>KF</given-names></name><name><surname>Crain</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cholera toxin-A subunit blocks opioid excitatory effects on sensory neuron action potentials indicating mediation by Gs-linked opioid receptors</article-title><source>Brain Res</source><year>1990</year><volume>525</volume><fpage>225</fpage><lpage>231</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2174711</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0006-8993(90)90868-C</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schultz</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenthal</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Hescheler</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Trautwein</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of G-Proteins in Calcium-Channel Modulation</article-title><source>Annual Review of Physiology</source><year>1990</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>275</fpage><lpage>292</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1691905</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1146/annurev.ph.52.030190.001423</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group pers